# AuthKit configuration for the console.
#
# Every variable here is PUBLIC. They are `PUBLIC_`-prefixed because Astro
# inlines them into the browser bundle at build time, and they are safe there:
# a WorkOS client ID travels in the authorization URL of every sign-in, and the
# browser SDK never touches an API key or a client secret. If a change ever
# needs one of those, it does not belong in this file — it belongs on a server.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored.

# The client ID of the "Mzizi Console" AuthKit application — each WorkOS
# environment holds several applications, and the environment's default one
# belongs to a different product, so use these, not the default:
#   Staging     client_01M28SHV347A1DQ60J9D0BJVV4
#   Production  client_01M28SBQ4PKNHNQRR14R2CFMT2
# Unset means the gate fails closed: it says so on the page and sign-in is
# disabled, rather than quietly letting everyone through.
PUBLIC_WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=client_01M28SHV347A1DQ60J9D0BJVV4

# The Authentication API hostname, ONLY when the WorkOS environment has a
# custom Auth API domain configured. Leave empty otherwise — WorkOS warns that
# "continuing to make requests to api.workos.com after a custom domain is
# configured for the Authentication API can result in issues", and the converse
# is just as broken.
#   Staging     (none configured)
#   Production  auth.mukoko.com
PUBLIC_WORKOS_API_HOSTNAME=

# The path of the page that completes the OAuth redirect. Must match the
# redirect URI registered in the WorkOS dashboard for this environment.
PUBLIC_WORKOS_CALLBACK_PATH=/callback

# Override where the refresh token is kept. Unset is correct almost always:
# the SDK uses localStorage on localhost/127.0.0.1 and an HttpOnly cookie
# everywhere else. Set to `true` only to reproduce the localhost behaviour on
# another host, and never for production — `true` puts the refresh token in
# localStorage, where any script on the page can read it.
PUBLIC_WORKOS_DEV_MODE=
